# Deployed Python function bundle exclusions.
#
# CORRECTION: an earlier version of this file also excluded data/chunks/.
# That was wrong and broke production (500s): on a read-only runtime,
# retrieval.lexical_backend.load_readonly_bm25s() deliberately re-reads
# data/chunks/**/*_chunks.jsonl and recomputes corpus_version() from it,
# then compares that hash to the one recorded in
# data/bm25s_index/corpus_version.json at the last `build_bm25s_index`
# run. That cross-check is what catches "ingested new filings but forgot
# to rebuild + redeploy the bm25s index" -- a real correctness guarantee,
# not incidental. data/chunks/ MUST stay in the deployed bundle.
#
# data/raw/**/metadata.json (and the already-gitignored data/sec_cache/,
# data/embeddings/) are the only genuinely runtime-unused paths: nothing
# in api/*.py or retrieval/*.py's request path reads data/raw. Excluding
# just these is safe but does not materially move the bundle-size needle
# (metadata.json files are a few hundred bytes each) -- the real fix for
# Wave 1's 238.39 MB / 225 MB cap overage has to come from trimming
# ingestion-only Python dependencies out of the deployed function instead.
data/raw/
data/sec_cache/
data/embeddings/
